From 50c4c102f1d022509276ca52ab377ecabe90530a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pm-official-id <pm-official-id@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:19:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] All ten ArchiveTune player design styles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The picker now carries ArchiveTune's full set — Classic, Modern, Minimal,
Cinematic, Little, Expressive, Immersive, Immersive Extended, Material
Extended, Editorial — alongside Lokal's modern player and its classic
screen (the first port's 'classic' key migrates there). Nine of the ten
render through one parameterized screen whose spec table follows the
traits that distinguish the originals: Little's tinted compactness with
progress across the art, Immersive Extended's full-bleed white-on-black,
Material Extended's artwork wash behind a tinted control card, Editorial's
left-set type on a quiet field. Immersive remains the modern screen with
edge-to-edge artwork. All twelve styles share the same playback wiring.

Verified on an emulator: Little and Editorial render as designed.
